    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters May 23rd with a clear offensive engine, led by **Corbin Carroll** (81.41) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (73.03). **Corbin Carroll** is our highest-rated asset today; his favorable spot in the #2 hole against Michael Lorenzen combined with strong xwOBA metrics makes him an essential anchor for our stolen base targets. **Tyler Soderstrom** also benefits significantly from a soft matchup against Lucas Giolito, whose 5.01 xERA provides a ceiling-raising environment for **Tyler Soderstrom**'s power potential. We are also looking for a productive day from **Brice Turang** (72.43), as his placement in the #2 slot against the high-strikeout risk of Roki Sasaki provides a rare opportunity to capitalize on base-running efficiency. \n\nEfficiency across the board remains our primary focus, with **James Wood** (70.10) and **Josh Naylor** (69.73) rounding out a solid top-tier. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (60.32) remains a start despite facing a tougher arm in Kirby, as his platoon advantage (R/L) offers enough of a buffer to maintain value. The most difficult decision rested on **Kyle Karros** (51.91), who sat just outside the primary lineup. While **Kyle Karros** offered respectable utility, the optimizer favored the platoon-leveraged plate appearances of **Gabriel Moreno** and the situational utility of our primary infielders. We continue to monitor the statuses of **Mickey Moniak** (IL) and **Jose Caballero** (Rainout), ensuring we maximize our remaining game caps while maintaining a high floor for the categories of R, HR, RBI, SB, and AVG.",
